          "requirement": "Enable the supported INI_ALLOW_NO_VALUE configuration so string parsing can invoke the name-only handler after an earlier parse error.",
          "target_route": "An accepted input such as `[broken\\nname` reaches LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput, then ini_parse_string and ini_parse_stream; the first line records an error and the second is a no-value name.",
          "failure_condition": "The recipe supplies no enabling definition, so INI_ALLOW_NO_VALUE defaults to 0 and the second line takes the error-only branch without invoking the handler.",
          "alternative_paths": "No input can enable a compile-time branch. The entry makes one parse-string call, and the recipe does not use the repository's enabling option.",
          "discovery_necessary": true,
          "discovery_established": true
        },
        {
          "candidate_id": "c2",
          "source_id": "no_value_handler_failure_coverage",
          "origin": "discover",
          "kind": "call",
          "change_ids": [
            "g0002"
          ],
          "requirement": "Exercise a no-value handler refusal after an earlier error to cover preservation of the first error.",
          "target_route": "With no-value handling enabled, a finite input containing a malformed section followed by a name-only line reaches the changed handler-failure guard when the target callback returns 0 for that name.",
          "failure_condition": "The old recipe disables no-value handling, and the old callback returns 1 for every invocation, so the guard's handler-failure behavior is never reached.",
          "alternative_paths": "Other parser error assignments do not execute this changed guard. Natural input cannot change the callback's constant return value or the compile-time default.",
          "discovery_necessary": true,
          "discovery_established": true
        }
      ],
